# Docker build context excludes (SMA-332: crates/paigasus-helikon-runtime-agentcore/docker/Dockerfile,
# built from the workspace root — see the crate's docker/Dockerfile header for the
# exact build command).
#
# A `cargo build -p paigasus-helikon-runtime-agentcore --example ...` build only
# needs the workspace's Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock plus every member crate's Cargo.toml
# and src/ tree. Everything below is either huge (a local `target/` directory can
# reach tens of GB) or irrelevant to compilation, and would otherwise be tar'd into
# the build context on every `docker build` invocation.
/target
.git
.superpowers
/docs
*.md

# Deliberately NOT copied into the build context: this repo's `rust-toolchain.toml`
# pins `channel = "stable"` (no exact version). If it were present in the builder
# image's working directory, rustup would try to resolve/fetch "stable" itself
# rather than using the version already baked into the `rust:<tag>-alpine` base
# image, adding a redundant network fetch and potentially a version mismatch
# against the tag pinned in the Dockerfile. Excluding it means the Dockerfile's
# base-image tag is the single source of truth for the toolchain version used to
# build the container image.
/rust-toolchain.toml
